# Production Scheduler: update both apps

Scheduler work is **not** single-repo. Apply the same functional change in **both** places and push **both** remotes.

## 1. Canonical scheduler app

- **Repo:** [Dharshantfs/production_scheduler](https://github.com/Dharshantfs/production_scheduler) — branch `main`
- **Local clone (this workspace):** `Planning/production_scheduler`

Implement Python/Vue/source changes here first (or here + entry in one session, but do not ship only one side).

## 2. Production Entry app (merged scheduler + desk)

- **Repo:** [Dharshantfs/production_entry_app](https://github.com/Dharshantfs/production_entry_app) — branch `master`
- **Local clone:** `PRODUCTION ENTRY/production_entry`

After scheduler logic/UI changes, **port** the same behaviour into `production_entry`:

- Bundled desk assets: `production_entry/production_entry/public/js/scheduler.bundle.js`, `public/css/scheduler.css` (rebuild from scheduler frontend when Vue/source changed)
- Server hooks/API used by the board: `production_entry/production_entry/production_planning/scheduler_api.py`, `scheduler_hooks.py`
- Vendored scheduler trees under the app root (keep in sync when they mirror the standalone app): `ps_full/production_scheduler/`, `production_scheduler_patch/production_scheduler/`

`production_entry/production_entry/hooks.py` loads `scheduler.bundle.js`; do not leave entry on an old bundle while only pushing `production_scheduler`.

## 3. Git pushes

- Push **production_scheduler** → `origin` on `production_scheduler` repo
- Push **production_entry** → `origin` on `production_entry_app` repo

## 4. Site note

If both `production_scheduler` and `production_entry` are installed on one site, hooks can overlap — `production_entry.install` logs when both are present. Prefer one installed app per site after validation.
